    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS), with `AcceptanceTest` being the only runnable test class (the other two files are the abstract `AcceptanceBase` and a non-test helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` rule: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing project conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator adds the field to the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that derives the tier from the owner's persisted `namesakeCount` and `email`, matching the existing computed-field pattern used for `displayName` and `initials`. Since both fields are stored on the owner, this evaluates correctly both at create time and on later `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass and the build is green.",
